course: dictionary
lesson: 11945
title: Boats, water and the word capsizing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Capsizing is a word about boats. When a boat capsizes, it turns over in the water, so the bottom of the boat ends up on top. The word comes from the verb capsize, which you can use in different forms: capsize, capsizes, capsized and capsizing.
explain: «The wind grew strong, and the little canoe began capsizing.» The wind is the cause, and the canoe turning over is what happens. Look at the words around capsizing to check: a strong wind and a canoe in water tell you it is a boat turning over, not a bird or a ball.
explain: Capsizing is a danger, so water safety lessons teach you what to do. «Always wear a life jacket, stay with the boat and keep calm.» Staying calm helps you think clearly and stay safe until help comes.
fact: Capsizing means turning over in the water, so the bottom of the boat is on top.
fact: Capsize is the verb. The forms are capsize, capsizes, capsized and capsizing.
fact: «Capsizing» can also mean making a boat turn over, as in «The big wave was capsizing the kayak.»
fact: Sailing clubs teach children capsizing on purpose, so they learn how to right the boat again.
fact: In water safety, a life jacket, staying with the boat and keeping calm are the best things to do if you capsize.
exercise: «The wind grew strong, and the little canoe began capsizing.» What does capsizing mean here? | Sailing very fast across the lake | *Turning over in the water | Dropping the anchor into the water | Stopping at the shore
exercise: Sam says capsizing means sinking to the bottom of the lake. What does capsizing really mean? | *Turning over in the water, so the bottom of the boat is on top | Parking the boat on the beach | Tying the boat to a tree | Making a noise like a whistle
exercise: In a sailing club, why do children practise capsizing on purpose? | To make the boat sink for fun | *To learn how to right the boat | To see the fish under the boat | To win a race against other boats
test: «Always wear a life jacket in case of capsizing.» What is the safety rule in this sentence? | Swim away from the boat as fast as you can | Take off your life jacket so you can swim faster | *Wear a life jacket to stay safe if the boat turns over | Only wear a life jacket on land
test: Which word is another form of capsize? | newspaper | lake | *capsized | canoe
exam: What is the best thing to do if your kayak starts capsizing? | Shout and wave your arms and climb on top of the boat | Take off your life jacket so you can swim better | *Wear your life jacket, stay with the boat and keep calm | Swim as fast as you can to land far away
